      <section class="project-section card" id="pihole">
        <h2>Pi-Hole</h2>

        <h3>What is Pi-Hole?</h3>
        <p>This is too much for me to explain. Go to the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pi-hole" target="_blank">Wiki page for PiHole</a> for more detailed info.</p>
        <p>TLDR - PiHole is an ad-blocker and allows for superior control over internet traffic and use in the home. It is open sourced and cool if you can figure it out.</p>

        <h3>How to do it?</h3>
        <p>Here are some YouTube videos and links explaining how to do it! You need a raspberry or some other computer that runs Linux. This computer will be running constantly so choose something that uses minimal power (i.e. raspberry pi).</p>

        <ul>
          <li>Here is the <a href="https://pi-hole.net/" target="_blank">Pi-Hole Website</a>.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="video-grid">
          <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/roYduABVjo8"></iframe>
          <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/xtMFcVx3cHU"></iframe>
          <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/cE21YjuaB6o"></iframe>
        </div>

        <p>Once you've fully set up the raspberry pi, Wi-Fi configuration settings, and pi-hole, you can start blocking what you want! Here are some links to blacklists for what I block and why; the rest you can google around for! These aren't all navigable links, so I'll put the in as text, and you can either add them to your ad-list (of things to blacklist) or go to them by copying and pasting.</p>

        <ul>
          <li>General - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/StevenBlack/hosts/master/hosts</li>
          <li>Tracking - https://s3.amazonaws.com/lists.disconnect.me/simple_tracking.txt</li>
          <li>Ads - https://s3.amazonaws.com/lists.disconnect.me/simple_ad.txt</li>
          <li>Adult Content - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chadmayfield/my-pihole-blocklists/master/lists/pi_blocklist_porn_all.list</li>
          <li>General - http://sysctl.org/cameleon/hosts</li>
          <li>SmartTV - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perflyst/PiHoleBlocklist/master/SmartTV.txt</li>
          <li>LG Tracking - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perflyst/PiHoleBlocklist/master/regex.list</li>
          <li>Safe Adlist - https://dbl.oisd.nl/</li>
          <li>Facebook - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aronjanosch/pihole-facebook_oculus/main/pihole-facebook.txt</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>My Pi-Hole</h3>
        <p>Here is what my pi-hole looks like. It requires that you have a raspberry pi or some computer that runs linux.</p>

        <div class="media-grid">
          <img src="/assets/img/my-pi-w-pihole-on-it.png" alt="my-pi-w-pihole-on-it" />
          <img src="/assets/img/pihole-login.png" alt="pihole-login" />
