      <section class="project-section card" id="homeServer">
        <h2>Home Server</h2>

        <h3>What is Home Serving/Self Hosting?</h3>
        <p>
          The concept in which you host your own applications, data, and more. Taking away the "unknown" factor in how your data is managed and stored, this provides those with the willingness to learn and the mind to do so to take control of their data without losing the functionality of services they otherwise use frequently.
          <br /><strong>Some Examples:</strong> For instance, if you use dropbox, but are not fond of having your most sensitive data stored in a data-storage container that you do not have direct control over, you may consider NextCloud. Or let's say you're used to hosting a blog out of a Blogger platform, but would rather have your own customization and flexibility of controlling your updates? Why not give WordPress a go. The possibilities are endless and it all starts here with a server.
        </p>

        <h3>How to do it?</h3>
        <p>I'm not entirely sure on the whole process. The <a href="https://adrift.space/r-selfhosted/wiki/" target="_blank">Wiki Page</a> for self-hosting has good information. Also, the subreddits <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/selfhosted/" target="_blank">r/selfhosted</a> and <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/HomeServer/" target="_blank">r/HomeServer</a> have lots of information and places to interact w/ community members who've paved the way and done this before.</p>

        <h3>My Server</h3>
        <p>I don't have one yet. This is my next side project!</p>
      </section>

      <section class="project-section card" id="wiiHomebrew">
        <h2>Wii/WiiU Homebrew</h2>

        <h3>What is homebrew?</h3>
        <p>Homebrew refers to software not authorized by Nintendo. This can include games, utilities, emulators and much more! Running homebrew on your Nintendo Wii can be done for free by exploiting bugs in Wii’s software. The modifications installed by following this guide will give you easy and persistent access to Wii homebrew.</p>

        <h3>How to do it?</h3>
        <p>Go <a href="https://wii.guide/get-started" target="_blank">here</a> and follow the steps from the exploit of your choosing. There are many to choose from, but I used the str2hax method to install the Homebrew channel on my Nintendo Wii.</p>
        <p>TLDR - You can modify your Wii to do cool things. Here's some videos to show why to do it followed by how.</p>

